    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0551" n="541" xml:id="pg541"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.002/11–548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-05T16:00:00+08:00">November 5, 1948—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 5—8:36 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2106. Foreign Minister Wang Shih-chieh informs us Cabinet, under urgent plea from
                        Generalissimo,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d437-f1"/> has agreed remain in power
                    few more days. There are afoot in high Government circles plans for “radical”
                    measures in desperate effort improve situation. Cabinet is remaining in power
                    pending final decision this problem.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d437-f1" n="33" xml:id="d437-f1-content">
                <p>Chiang Kai-shek, President of the Republic of China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
